{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/942596-creating-enemies-in-nwod","id":942596,"title":"Creating enemies in nWoD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-03T02:58:39-07:00","id":942596,"title":"Creating enemies in nWoD","content":"Hi there,<br /> <br /> I've glossed over the forums here and couldn't find anything exactly related to what I need help with. However if I've missed something or there is a thread for this already please do point me in the right direction <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In any case, I'll soon be running a nWoD game where the characters are mortal but will be encountering otherworldly creatures that they will probably have to fight. The creatures in question are somewhere between demonic and eldritch in nature and honestly I'm not sure where to start when it comes to figuring out their stats and abilities. I have some NPC characters that have supernatural abilities so I've just cherry picked things from Mage: the awakening that will suit my game. However, when it comes to the enemies I have no point of reference to work from, and as far as I can tell there is not a monster manual akin to D&amp;D that I can pull from. <br /> <br /> Does anyone have any tips for creating creatures, or know if any of the other variations of WoD have anything I could work from. I've had a look over the Inferno book but there are no example enemies with stat blocks laid out like in the 2nd edition nWoD book with the example thugs/police etc.<br /> <br /> Any help or advice would be most appreciated.<br /> <br /> Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12223-k00patrooper","name":"k00patrooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T03:26:31-07:00","id":942608,"title":"","content":"Have you read &quot;Horrors and Wonders: Antagonists&quot; chapter in CofD corebook?<br /> Also check this thread below, Reighnell is really great at creating horrors.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...he-horror-show</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 08-03-2016, 06:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T03:39:18-07:00","id":942614,"title":"","content":"Are you aware of the Horror creation rules?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T04:12:35-07:00","id":942629,"title":"","content":"Ah no I was working from the 2nd edition book and not the new Chronicles of Darkness rulebook. I didn't know there was a new section dedicated to exactly this in there. I'll pick it up now. Also the thread you linked looks really helpful, thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12223-k00patrooper","name":"k00patrooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T06:57:53-07:00","id":942683,"title":"","content":"There is also the Antagonists book, and the various Night Horrors books. All 1E, thus far, but the basics can be harvested and updated without too much effort. If the Horrors section in the CofD Core book doesn't work for you.<br /> <br /> As far as the Eldritch and Demon-y goes, Night Horrors: the Unbidden (Mage) for Abyssals, and Night Horrors: Wolfsbane (Werewolf) for Idigam work well. Mummy has some Eldritch Horror buried in it, Pandorans from Promethean can model the common Body Horror feel well.<br /> <br /> Just remembered: Inferno has the more common, modern perception of Demons down well, Second Sight has a good chapter on Cults and Things That Should Not Be.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And remember that Spirits and even Angels can easily be cast in the Eldritch Horror light. Both already have alien mindsets and strange powers. The PCs would know the sources of them, nor the differences, so it's all frighteningly strange to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":".  Additional ideas 08-03-2016, 10:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T09:23:17-07:00","id":942754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>k00patrooper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/942596-creating-enemies-in-nwod?p=942629#post942629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah no I was working from the 2nd edition book and not the new Chronicles of Darkness rulebook.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean the God Machine's Chronicle?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T13:37:07-07:00","id":942959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/942596-creating-enemies-in-nwod?p=942683#post942683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is also the Antagonists book, and the various Night Horrors books. All 1E, thus far, but the basics can be harvested and updated without too much effort. If the Horrors section in the CofD Core book doesn't work for you.<br /> <br /> As far as the Eldritch and Demon-y goes, Night Horrors: the Unbidden (Mage) for Abyssals, and Night Horrors: Wolfsbane (Werewolf) for Idigam work well. Mummy has some Eldritch Horror buried in it, Pandorans from Promethean can model the common Body Horror feel well.<br /> <br /> Just remembered: Inferno has the more common, modern perception of Demons down well, Second Sight has a good chapter on Cults and Things That Should Not Be.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And remember that Spirits and even Angels can easily be cast in the Eldritch Horror light. Both already have alien mindsets and strange powers. The PCs would know the sources of them, nor the differences, so it's all frighteningly strange to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rad. Thank you so much. I think I'll stick to some simple archetypes for now and read the stuff you recommended and maybe fold it into what I've got planned <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12223-k00patrooper","name":"k00patrooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T13:38:06-07:00","id":942961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/942596-creating-enemies-in-nwod?p=942754#post942754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You mean the God Machine's Chronicle?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Naw just the nWorld of Darkness core book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12223-k00patrooper","name":"k00patrooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T14:24:10-07:00","id":942992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>k00patrooper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/942596-creating-enemies-in-nwod?p=942961#post942961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Naw just the nWorld of Darkness core book.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Chronicles of Darkness rulebook IS the 2nd edition corebook...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\